From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leszek Swirski <leszeks@chromium.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:49:16 +0200
Subject: [interpreter] Avoid emitting switches and jump tables in dead code

Previously, allocating a jump table and binding its entries in dead
code (such as in a `switch`, `yield`, `yield*`, or `try`-`finally`
after an unconditional exit like `with (o) { return; }`) left an
unemitted switch while still binding jump table targets and starting
new basic blocks in unreachable code.

Check RemainderOfBlockIsDead() before allocating jump tables or
emitting switches in BytecodeGenerator, and DCHECK in
AllocateJumpTable and CHECK in WriteSwitch that the current block is
not dead.

TAG=agy
CONV=1dd9fbe9-ef03-4efb-85db-698730a3015f

Fixed: 568794851
Change-Id: I4f59887fe59243966d94f3d014c894d297eb7ab5
